{"at":"2026-10-15T17:49:59.965Z","ms":264,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-cursor","note":"Usage: put it over footage with the footage item's transform; give it the recording's sidecar as is. { \"asset\": \"kit-cursor\", \"start\": 0, \"duration\": 10.4, \"transform\": <footage item's>, \"params\": { \"path\": <sidecar.cursor>, \"clicks\": <sidecar.clicks>, \"at\": 0, \"speed\": 1 } }. With footage trimmed in: 2, use at: 2; if the footage has a kit-camera motion, give the cursor the same motion."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:00.374Z","ms":264,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-spotlight","note":"Usage: dims all but an element box from the recording's sidecar, in the picture's pixels (space 1440x900 by default). { \"asset\": \"kit-spotlight\", \"start\": 3, \"duration\": 3, \"transform\": <footage's>, \"params\": { \"region\": { \"x\": 24, \"y\": 524, \"width\": 228, \"height\": 30 }, \"padding\": 10 } }. Several regions in turn: \"regions\": [{ \"t\": 3.34, ...box }]."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:00.786Z","ms":262,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-camera","note":"Usage: a motion on the footage item (and on the cursor and spotlight over it): \"motions\": [{ \"asset\": \"kit-camera\", \"phase\": \"emphasis\", \"at\": 3.3, \"duration\": 2.6, \"params\": { \"region\": { ...box }, \"fill\": 0.6 } }]. Set anchorX, anchorY and itemScale to the item's transform. Mask the footage to its box (mask transform fixed) so the zoom stays inside it."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:01.194Z","ms":261,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-arrow","note":"Usage: { \"asset\": \"kit-arrow\", \"start\": 6, \"duration\": 2.6, \"transform\": <footage's>, \"params\": { \"from\": { \"x\": 980, \"y\": 640 }, \"to\": { \"x\": 1135, \"y\": 540 }, \"label\": \"Open it\" } } (points in the picture's pixels)."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:01.600Z","ms":264,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-callout","note":"Usage: a short label that points at a place in the picture and stays inside the safe area. { \"asset\": \"kit-callout\", \"start\": 4.2, \"duration\": 2.8, \"transform\": <footage's>, \"params\": { \"text\": \"Filter by *kind*\", \"point\": { \"x\": 138, \"y\": 539 }, \"side\": \"auto\" } }."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:02.012Z","ms":260,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-ui-frame","note":"Usage: a browser (or phone, tablet) around a capture: { \"asset\": \"kit-ui-frame\", \"start\": 0, \"duration\": 10, \"transform\": { \"width\": 0.9, \"height\": 0.9 }, \"params\": { \"device\": \"browser\", \"content\": \"studio-library-search\", \"url\": \"127.0.0.1:8787\", \"title\": \"Library\" } }. scale: 1 draws the capture pixel for pixel (crisp UI); overlays placed on the frame's box do not know where its viewport is, so annotate footage placed on its own instead."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:02.432Z","ms":268,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-plate","note":"Usage: the plate behind a group (chart, steps, a headline): { \"asset\": \"kit-plate\", \"start\": 0.4, \"duration\": 6, \"params\": { \"eyebrow\": \"Growth\", \"title\": \"Views, *doubled*\" }, \"transform\": { \"space\": \"safe\", \"x\": 0.5, \"y\": 0.5, \"width\": 0.9, \"height\": 0.8 } }."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:02.848Z","ms":259,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-steps","note":"Usage: steps walked while the narration goes through them: { \"asset\": \"kit-steps\", \"start\": 1, \"duration\": 8, \"params\": { \"steps\": [\"Upload\", \"Describe\", \"Build\", \"Render\"], \"at\": [0.5, 2.5, 4.5, 6.5] } }; or keyframe params.current. A column fits a side panel; the extra at time ticks the last step."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:03.250Z","ms":259,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"kit-icon","note":"Usage: one Lucide icon (ISC) by name: { \"asset\": \"kit-icon\", \"start\": 1.2, \"duration\": 4, \"params\": { \"name\": \"rocket\", \"weight\": 2, \"draw\": 0.8 } }. Names are Lucide's own (house, pencil, trash-2); one weight across a video."},"ok":true}
{"at":"2026-10-15T17:50:03.659Z","ms":264,"kind":"tool","name":"add_asset_note","args":{"name":"end-card","note":"v3: add cta (a button), url and logoMode: svg for an uploaded SVG logo drawn as vectors; with those left out it draws exactly like v2. clipTheme: true reads the clip's theme instead of the theme param."},"ok":true}
